\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces High-level architecture and request flow. Discord commands, HTTP requests, and the background monitor all converge on the shared agent workflow layer, which holds two agents: a read-only investigator and a gated remediator. The workflow drives read-only tools and the LLM, persists incidents and pending remediation approvals to SQLite, and posts alerts to Discord. The dashed feedback edge shows the monitor escalating a down endpoint or firing alert rule to the alerting layer, routed along the top margin to avoid crossing other boxes. The remediation agent writes only a pending approval; execution of a restart is gated by a human approval (not shown) before it reaches the Docker daemon.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{6}{High-level architecture and request flow. Discord commands, HTTP requests, and the background monitor all converge on the shared agent workflow layer, which holds two agents: a read-only investigator and a gated remediator. The workflow drives read-only tools and the LLM, persists incidents and pending remediation approvals to SQLite, and posts alerts to Discord. The dashed feedback edge shows the monitor escalating a down endpoint or firing alert rule to the alerting layer, routed along the top margin to avoid crossing other boxes. The remediation agent writes only a pending approval; execution of a restart is gated by a human approval (not shown) before it reaches the Docker daemon}{figure.1}{}}
